lane: channel-weak-gap
why: okayWeak 206us vs zioWeak 169us. The profile names three costs,
     not one, and the first is a methodology fault: ZStream.fromQueue
     takes up to maxChunkSize (4096) elements per queue operation
     while our consumer calls receiveBlocking once per element. Before
     any mechanism claim, both sides must be measured at BOTH
     granularities: an elementwise ZIO lane (q.take in a loop) and a
     chunked okay lane (receiveManyAsync draining the ring in bulk).
     The other two costs are ours to remove: two allocations per
     element on the callback path (boxToBoolean 8% of leaf samples,
     Right(Some(a)) 3.4%) and the CompletableFuture handshake in
     CanBlock.block (~12%) which allocates and calls get() even when
     the callback already fired synchronously.
